[about]
Title=02 - User Interface Concepts
Intro=What _APP_ is made of, each part named by the narrator and then shown by the screen reader: its window, its main view, its dialogs, its status, its menus, and its help.
Setup=_APP_ is installed and your reader is running.
Homework=Open _APP_ and, as each part takes focus, listen for its name, its kind, its value or state, and the hint after a pause.

[step]

Say=Each part I name, the reader then shows: the name, the kind of control, its value and state, and a hint. First, the window. Its desktop key brings _APP_ forward, never a second copy.
Key=Alt+Control+<letter>
Hear=_APP_
Hear=<the program's own greeting, if it has one>

[step]

Say=The title, then the greeting. Next, the main view, a control the reader already knows.
Key=
Hear=<name>, <role>, <value or state>
Hear=<the hint, such as Type in text.>

[step]

Say=Name, role, value, then the hint. Dialogs all work one way: a label, then its control.
Key=<the key that opens a dialog>
Hear=<title> dialog
Hear=<label>: <role>
Hear=<the hint>

[step]

Say=Tab moves on; at the end come OK and Cancel. Enter is OK, Escape is Cancel, Control plus Enter submits from anywhere.
Key=Tab
Hear=OK button
Hear=To activate press Spacebar.

[step]

Say=The status asks and changes nothing: Shift plus Z.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=<the status line, word for word>

[step]

Say=Menus say their keys. F10 opens the menu bar.
Key=F10
Hear=Menu bar
Hear=<first menu> menu

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the part; the reader says the key.
Key=
Hear=
